    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "FINAL OFFERS BY 12PM ON FRIDAY 9TH OCTOBER 2026\nPrime property to come to market comprising derelict cottage and granary, altogether standing on c. 28.02 Acres of lands located at end of country lane c. 3 kilometres from Curraghboy and c. 5 kilometres from Brideswell. Holding huge potential for re-development, the residence is suitable for qualification for the Vacant Home Grant. The lands are predominantly good quality, front onto the Cross River and possess an ideal opportunity for local farmers to increase their existing holdings. Folio RN22941.\nThe Auctioneer invites enquiries and offers for immediate sale.\nFor further details, contact DNG Ivan Connaughton on 090-6663700.\nDirections:\nFrom Curraghboy, take Brideswell/Athlone Road, turn right at end of village, proceed for c. 2 kilometres, turn right, proceed for c. 600 metres, property located to front at end of road. (Note For Sale signs at junctions and on property)"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Notice\nPlease note we have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings, or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. All measurements are approximate and photographs provided for guidance only."
      },
